  "body": "Production can have the imported-event suppression migration recorded before the older metadata-visibility migration arrives. Applying the missing migration drops suppression filtering; the reverse order drops metadata privacy. The release schema gate stopped the observed rollout after migrations committed, before any image change.\n\nAdds an immutable forward migration composing both boundaries and requires both in release verification. Existing migration checksums and source data remain unchanged. The automatic production-schema gate now reproduces both historical overwrites, rejects each, repairs twice, and verifies public/private/suppressed events, cached search, and venue projections.\n\nValidation: local PostgreSQL 16 passed all 103 migrations, both historical-order repairs, rollback-only synthetic projection checks, and backend boot/restart idempotence. Repository quality and formal checks passed. CI must pass this exact revision before merging.\n\nRecovery: the failed rollout retained the original API image. The previously deployed suppression view was restored after matching its ledger checksum; four newly introduced RSVP capabilities were temporarily disabled because the old binary rejects them. Restore those four capabilities only after every machine runs compatible code. A rollback to the old image requires disabling them first. Keep discovery and PayPal intake at their original settings. Full evidence and C04 acceptance are in docs/critical-completion-2026-09-16.md.\n\nDepends on merged #336 and #418. Use a merge commit to preserve the migration introduction commit referenced by the manifest.\n\n\n\n## Production delivery evidence \u2014 2026-09-17\n\nDeployed merged revision `9f0da14de84919f8fba391fa752b7df7412a600d` to both Fly `tdf-hq` machines (ord/lax) using `scripts/production-release.mjs` after [merged-revision CI/image](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/actions/runs/35238806594) succeeded. Verified amd64 digest `sha256:fd7a015858ff34df984a718097afddae22500c21282bfa4434aafeeff39a594d`, per-machine health/version, all 103 migrations and full schema gate, zero release leases, zero private/suppressed public-event rows, and restored discovery/RSVP. Maintenance completed at 15:31:33Z. PayPal intake remained enabled; refunds/Datafast remained disabled. No live payment or invitation mutation was used.\n\nAuthorized browser smoke: health/version200; Admin invitation list200 with78 rows for event86; anonymous list401; logistics200 with expected shape. Worker configuration present; 100-line operational sample had zero worker tick failures/disabled warnings; provider queue empty. Local regression/CI remain the evidence for injected logging failures and transactional concurrency.\n\nC01/C02/C03/C04 meet delivery acceptance. On 2026-09-17 at 20:43:56Z, a newly created synthetic account authenticated through the normal signup/login endpoints with only the Customer role. In an isolated browser context on production revision 9f0da14de84919f8fba391fa752b7df7412a600d, event86 returned200, isOrganizer was false, and its invitation list returned200 with zero rows. The same request without authentication returned401; /admin/users returned403. The original Admin browser session remained intact. No invitation was created or modified, and no password/token/message contents were printed. The application subsequently confirmed the same Customer session. C01 final production acceptance is complete; no critical-scope blocker remains.\n\nThe first release attempt failed schema verification before image changes and temporarily disrupted startup of the original image. Recovery and the exact RSVP/refund-constraint compatibility requirements are documented in `docs/critical-completion-2026-09-16.md`. The corrected release completed without rollback. Required reviews/checks and migration ancestry were respected.\n\n",
